{"name":"Fancy Red Wine","hex":"#b40441","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"fancy","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The imagination.","An image or representation of anything formed in the mind."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Decorative, or featuring decorations, especially intricate or diverse ones.","Of a superior grade."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fancy"},{"term":"red","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of the setting sun, blood, and strawberries; the color which is evoked by the longest visible wavelengths (between about 625–740 nm), and a primary additive color.","A revolutionary socialist or (most commonly) a Communist;  a Bolshevik, a supporter of the Bolsheviks in the Russian Civil War."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a red hue.","Having an orange-brown or orange-blond colour; ginger."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red"},{"term":"wine","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An alcoholic beverage made by fermenting grape juice, with an ABV ranging from 5.5–16%.","An alcoholic beverage made by fermenting other substances, producing a similar ABV."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To entertain (someone) with wine.","To drink wine."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wine"}],"entries":[{"title":"Fancy (singer)","blocks":[{"text":"Manfred Alois Segieth, better known by his stage name Fancy, is a German singer, songwriter, and record producer. His greatest success came in the 1980s as a singer of the Eurodisco genre, with songs like \"Flames of Love\", \"Slice Me Nice\", \"Bolero \", \"Chinese Eyes\", or \"Lady of Ice\" being chart hits in numerous countries across the world."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/Fancy20090218.jpg/330px-Fancy20090218.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fancy_(singer)"},{"title":"Red wine","blocks":[{"text":"Red wine is a type of wine made from dark-colored grape varieties. The color of the wine can range from intense violet, typical of young wines, through to brick red for mature wines and brown for older red wines. The juice from most purple grapes is greenish-white, the red color coming from anthocyan pigments present in the skin of the grape. Much of the red wine production process involves extraction of color and flavor components from the grape skin."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/c/c0/Red_Wine_Glass.jpg/330px-Red_Wine_Glass.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red_wine"},{"title":"Wine","blocks":[{"text":"Wine is an alcoholic drink made from fermented grape juice. It is produced and consumed in many regions around the world, in a wide variety of styles which are influenced by different varieties of grapes, growing environments, viticulture methods, and production techniques."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Red_and_white_wine_in_glass.jpg/330px-Red_and_white_wine_in_glass.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wine"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Fancy-03a.jpg/500px-Fancy-03a.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Fancy-03a.jpg/500px-Fancy-03a.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Fancy in 1987","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFancy-03a.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/DSCN4149_%281%29.jpg/500px-DSCN4149_%281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/DSCN4149_%281%29.jpg/1280px-DSCN4149_%281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/DSCN4149_%281%29.jpg/500px-DSCN4149_%281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Fancy in 2021","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADSCN4149_(1).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/Four_colors_of_wine.png/500px-Four_colors_of_wine.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/Four_colors_of_wine.png/500px-Four_colors_of_wine.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Simplified illustration of the four colors of wine – red wine, orange wine, rosé wine, white wine","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFour_colors_of_wine.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Ros%C3%A9_wine_-_July_2023_-_Sarah_Stierch_01-cropped.jpg/500px-Ros%C3%A9_wine_-_July_2023_-_Sarah_Stierch_01-cropped.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/